WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:12.030
Cooking class was over.

2
00:00:15.553 --> 00:00:18.115
As Jason hung up his apron, his phone beeped.

3
00:00:19.136 --> 00:00:20.397
So did his friends' phones.

4
00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:23.460
"It's a video from Ethan!"

5
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:24.661
Jason said.

6
00:00:26.282 --> 00:00:28.004
As he played it, everyone watched.

7
00:00:29.864 --> 00:00:31.305
Even Chef was interested.

8
00:00:31.325 --> 00:00:35.267
"It's Ethan surfing," Bobby said.

9
00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:37.909
"He's a great athlete."

10
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.351
"He's so tanned!"

11
00:00:41.731 --> 00:00:42.411
Nina said.

12
00:00:44.112 --> 00:00:44.893
Izzie sighed.

13
00:00:44.913 --> 00:00:48.575
"Isn't he cool?"

14
00:00:49.575 --> 00:00:50.796
Jason rolled his eyes.

15
00:00:50.816 --> 00:00:54.118
"I bet he wiped out a lot before this video."

16
00:00:54.138 --> 00:00:57.900
"You're just jealous," Izzie said.

17
00:00:59.484 --> 00:01:01.005
Ethan sent another video.

18
00:01:02.006 --> 00:01:05.308
In this one, he was ordering fish tacos from a food truck.

19
00:01:06.309 --> 00:01:09.731
His text said, Hope everyone is having a great summer!

20
00:01:09.751 --> 00:01:12.974
"Hmm," Chef said.

21
00:01:12.994 --> 00:01:16.756
"Why don't we make fish tacos in our next class?"

22
00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.920
Everyone cheered, except for Jason.

23
00:01:24.622 --> 00:01:27.604
The next day Jason was excited to show off his new look.

24
00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:32.150
He felt cool in his sunglasses, tank top, and flip-flops.

25
00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:37.193
"Maybe nobody will notice my sunburn," he thought.

26
00:01:41.795 --> 00:01:43.736
His friends stared at him as he walked in.

27
00:01:44.997 --> 00:01:46.297
But nobody said anything.

28
00:01:48.058 --> 00:01:49.439
Chef pointed to the screen.

29
00:01:49.459 --> 00:01:52.140
"There's our fish taco recipe.

30
00:01:53.201 --> 00:01:54.722
Let's start chopping vegetables."

31
00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.524
The kids chopped cabbage and red onion.

32
00:02:00.312 --> 00:02:02.533
"Jason, you're sunburned!"

33
00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:03.594
Nina said.

34
00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:05.675
Izzie frowned.

35
00:02:05.695 --> 00:02:08.837
"Sunburn harms your skin.

36
00:02:09.697 --> 00:02:11.238
You should wear sunscreen."

37
00:02:12.419 --> 00:02:13.379
Jason shrugged.

38
00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.421
"I was just soaking up some rays."

39
00:02:16.441 --> 00:02:20.623
"Jason, please juice the lime," Chef said.

40
00:02:20.643 --> 00:02:23.625
"And take off those sunglasses."

41
00:02:25.246 --> 00:02:26.287
"I can see fine."

42
00:02:26.307 --> 00:02:28.328
"Take them off!

43
00:02:29.632 --> 00:02:30.953
You don't need them inside."

44
00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:35.155
Jason sighed and put on his regular glasses.

45
00:02:36.235 --> 00:02:38.236
He had white circles around his eyes.

46
00:02:40.117 --> 00:02:41.037
Bobby chuckled.

47
00:02:41.057 --> 00:02:44.599
"Nice look!"

48
00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.481
Jason ignored him and juiced the lime.

49
00:02:50.262 --> 00:02:52.263
Then he poured the juice over the vegetables.

50
00:02:53.743 --> 00:02:55.084
Izzie added sour cream.

51
00:02:57.108 --> 00:03:00.089
Nina sprinkled in salt and stirred the ingredients together.

52
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.651
Bobby put the bowl in the refrigerator to chill.

53
00:03:04.671 --> 00:03:10.373
"Now we mix the spices for the fish," Chef said.

54
00:03:12.394 --> 00:03:13.975
Bobby measured garlic powder.

55
00:03:16.016 --> 00:03:17.496
Nina poured in cumin.

56
00:03:19.597 --> 00:03:21.438
Jason measured the cayenne pepper.

57
00:03:23.679 --> 00:03:26.760
Izzie added salt and black pepper, and stirred everything.

58
00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.261
Chef seasoned the fish.

59
00:03:36.704 --> 00:03:40.666
Izzie added oil to a pan and turned the heat to medium-high.

60
00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:44.428
"Nina, please chop cilantro," Chef said.

61
00:03:44.448 --> 00:03:46.810
"Bobby, cut lime wedges."

62
00:03:52.012 --> 00:03:53.033
Chef cooked the fish.

63
00:03:54.614 --> 00:03:56.315
Then he put the fillets on a plate.

64
00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:59.589
"Izzie and Jason, break these into pieces."

65
00:04:01.551 --> 00:04:03.012
Jason gave him a thumbs-up.

66
00:04:03.032 --> 00:04:05.294
"Sure thing, dude."

67
00:04:06.595 --> 00:04:08.337
The other kids burst out laughing.

68
00:04:08.357 --> 00:04:12.120
"What's so funny?"

69
00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:13.522
Jason snapped.

70
00:04:14.583 --> 00:04:17.385
"You're not being yourself," Bobby said.

71
00:04:18.426 --> 00:04:19.387
Jason frowned.

72
00:04:19.407 --> 00:04:22.089
"I'm tired of being myself.

73
00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.752
I'm trying something new."

74
00:04:30.408 --> 00:04:33.889
Chef heated another pan and warmed the tortillas on both sides.

75
00:04:33.909 --> 00:04:37.850
"Now we can build our tacos."

76
00:04:39.451 --> 00:04:42.371
The kids put the vegetables and fish into the warm tortillas.

77
00:04:43.452 --> 00:04:46.472
They each added cilantro and a squeeze of lime.

78
00:04:50.474 --> 00:04:51.634
Nina looked at Jason.

79
00:04:51.654 --> 00:04:54.655
"Trying new things is fine.

80
00:04:54.675 --> 00:04:59.016
I used to play the flute, but now I'm learning piano."

81
00:05:00.608 --> 00:05:03.890
"Just whatever you do, be yourself," Izzie said.

82
00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.191
Jason took a bite of taco.

83
00:05:08.152 --> 00:05:09.592
It was crunchy and delicious.

84
00:05:09.612 --> 00:05:12.834
"I guess you're right," he said.

85
00:05:12.854 --> 00:05:15.775
"I feel silly trying Ethan things.

86
00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.897
Next time I'll try new Jason things."

87
00:05:20.677 --> 00:05:21.578
Bobby grinned.

88
00:05:21.598 --> 00:05:25.520
"Sounds like a wise idea, dude!"
